                                    <h1>Restaurant Technology Stack: POS, KDS, Kitchen Ops Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Restaurant tech has become one of the most-invested vertical SaaS categories globally. A modern restaurant stack integrates POS + KDS + delivery + inventory + loyalty + accounting into one operational nervous system. Here is what to buy, what to build, and how to sequence.</p>
                                    <h2>The Restaurant Stack Components</h2>
                                    <p><strong>POS:</strong> Toast (USA), Petpooja / POSist / Rista (India), Foodics (UAE / GCC), Lightspeed (global). Order taking, payments, table management.<br><strong>KDS (Kitchen Display System):</strong> orders to kitchen screens, station-by-station routing, timing.<br><strong>Delivery integration:</strong> Zomato / Swiggy (India), Talabat / Careem / Deliveroo (UAE), DoorDash / Uber Eats (USA/global).<br><strong>Inventory + stock:</strong> ingredient-level tracking, recipe costing, waste tracking.<br><strong>Loyalty + CRM:</strong> customer database, reservation, marketing.<br><strong>Accounting:</strong> daily sales sync to Tally / QuickBooks / Xero.<br><strong>Staff scheduling:</strong> shift management, tip pooling.</p>
                                    <h2>Build vs Buy</h2>
                                    <p>Restaurant tech is dominated by strong SaaS providers. Custom build only for: large chain (100+ outlets) with unique operational model, specialty (cloud kitchen, dark kitchen, delivery-only) that off-shelf poorly supports, or B2B restaurant tech company building for the industry.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost Bands</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Single outlet (SaaS + hardware):</strong> ₹35K-150K one-time hardware + ₹3K-15K/month SaaS.<br><strong>Chain (10-50 outlets):</strong> ₹5-25 lakh one-time + ₹40K-200K/month.<br><strong>Enterprise chain (100+ outlets) custom build:</strong> ₹80 lakh - 3 Cr build + ongoing ops team.</p>
                                    <h2>The Delivery Integration Reality</h2>
                                    <p>Zomato / Swiggy / Talabat / Careem integrations are critical but painful — each has its own API, order flow, and cancellation logic. Middleware providers (Urbanpiper, Fooda, Openbook) reduce integration burden. Direct integration only if scale justifies it.</p>
                                    <h2>Cloud Kitchen Considerations</h2>
                                    <p>Cloud kitchens have different needs: multi-brand under one kitchen, dispatch to multiple delivery platforms, virtual brand management, food cost per virtual brand. Standard restaurant POS doesn't cover this well; specialised platforms (Cloud Kitchens' Otter, Urbanpiper, Petpooja Cloud) are worth the switch.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
